# hwrev.ini -- manual board override for RK3566
#
# Rename to hwrev.ini in the root of this (FAT) partition to use it.
#
# U-Boot identifies the device from SARADC channels 0 and 1 (and, for the RG
# DS and RG DS Plus, the RAM size) and sets the variables below.  If it picks the wrong board,
# name the right one here.  Every line is a U-Boot command, run right after
# detection, so anything set here wins.
#
# THE SHORT FORM: name the board and nothing else.
#
#   setenv hwrev rg-ds-plus
#
# U-Boot then applies that board's whole profile and throws the SARADC result
# away.  Prefer this over listing the variables by hand: a file that corrects
# hwrev but forgets dtb_kernel leaves the device running half one board's
# settings and half another's.  Boards with a profile:
#
#   rg-arc-s  powkiddy-rgb30  miniloong  powkiddy-x55  rg-ds  rg-ds-plus
#   miyoo-flip
#
# Lines after the board name still override individual variables:
#
#   hwrev       board name; reaches Linux as board=<hwrev>
#   dtb_uboot   DTB U-Boot uses for its own display/charge init; path included,
#               normally dtbs/<name>.dtb on this partition
#   dtb_kernel  DTB handed to Linux, a file name in fdts/
#   fb_rotate   console rotation: 0, 1, 2 or 3
#
# To find your device's ADC values, watch the serial console for:
#   hwrev: saradc ch0=<value> ch1=<value>, <RAM> MiB -> <board>

# Example: force the Anbernic RG DS Plus
#
#setenv hwrev rg-ds-plus
